@startuml
' Supporting record: lesson-side-chat-workflow.md
' Accepted manual interaction design; report arrival order is illustrative.
title Lesson and side-chat workflow: shared materials, separate responsibilities
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F4F4
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActorBorderColor #555555
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

actor Learner
participant Planner
participant "Lesson chat" as Lesson
participant "Side chat" as Side

Planner --> Learner: One flat upload set\nShared sources and lesson identifiers\nTwo role instructions
Learner -> Lesson: Attach files; send "Go"
Lesson --> Learner: Teach and assess\nPresent sources before questions

opt Learner uses a side chat
  Learner -> Side: Attach the same files;\nsend "Side chat"
  loop Learner asks a question
    Learner -> Side: Ask for clarification or depth
    Side --> Learner: Explain with source context\nand useful diagrams
  end
  note over Learner, Side
    Answer freely when asked;
    record help related to an assessment.
  end note
  Learner -> Side: Request supplemental report
  Side --> Learner: Questions, explanations, gaps,\nand assessment-related help
end

Lesson --> Learner: Main assessment report
Learner -> Planner: Return main report
Planner -> Planner: Validate and record\nreported assessment evidence

opt Supplemental report returned, now or later
  Learner -> Planner: Return side-chat report
  Planner -> Planner: Link explanations and help\nwithout duplicating assessment
end

note over Learner, Planner
  Report order is illustrative; either may arrive first.
  Main report can close the lesson packet.
  Side report alone does not certify independent understanding.
end note

Planner --> Learner: Recommend follow-up\nwithin the approved plan
@enduml
